        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x1000b2338",
        "observation": "IOServiceNameMatching followed by IORegistryEntrySearchCFProperty in IODeviceTree for local-mac-address; copies six canonical-order bytes."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x10034941c",
        "observation": "XPC com.apple.BlueTool RunBuiltinScript with script and optional btaddress; result checked by caller."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x10034a1bc",
        "observation": "Boot method may invoke script boot; init/deepsleep methods at0x10034aac8/0x10034ab6c use the same XPC path."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x1004a861c",
        "observation": "Initialization includes a failure branch for unknown platform/chipset/manufacturer; VM skip is separate and is not used by this driver."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100211ad8",
        "observation": "Parses BT_HCI_TRANSPORT as transport:driver:argument. H4 table is at0x1009bfd40; POSIX driver table is at0x1009bfc40."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100116c60",
        "observation": "POSIX driver opens PF_SYSTEM/SOCK_STREAM/SYSPROTO_CONTROL, resolves a supplied control name with CTLIOCGINFO, and uses Skywalk only for the exact default com.apple.uart.sk.bluetooth. Other names use read/write and termios socket options."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100117624",
        "observation": "Without an os_channel, HCI bytes are sent with write on the control socket."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100117920",
        "observation": "Without an os_channel, HCI bytes are received with read on the control socket."
      },
      {
        "image": "BlueTool",
        "address": "0x10003fcb0",
        "observation": "Dispatches kMsgId=RunBuiltinScript and kMsgArgs={script,btaddress}; replies with result/manufacturer/firmware; boot/init have 30 s timers and deepsleep 4 s."
      },
      {
        "image": "BlueTool",
        "address": "0x10003e1e0",
        "observation": "Native manufacturer selection uses Apple hardware/MobileGestalt vendor tags, not the HCI Company Identifier."
      },
      {
        "image": "BlueTool",
        "address": "0x1000131e0",
        "observation": "Native built-in firmware/script selection requires a platform/chip/vendor match."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x1003498b0",
        "observation": "Result zero advances boot; 10/13 indicate unsupported hardware; reads firmware and manufacturer into state/metrics."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x1001a071c",
        "observation": "Reads four bytes of transport-encoding from the bluetooth or marconi-bt DeviceTree node independently of BT_HCI_TRANSPORT."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100379ac4",
        "observation": "Chip model factory selects Apple-supported device profiles through MobileGestalt, plus ACI/VM overrides; no WCN3990 profile was found."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x1002229b0",
        "observation": "Vendor configuration rejects IDs beyond the native 1..6000 range."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x10022288c",
        "observation": "Vendor dispatch initializes BCM, ACI or SRS function tables by internal chipset-ID ranges; no QCA table."
      },
      {
        "image": "bluetoothd",
        "address": "0x100223034",
        "observation": "An absent vendor hook returns native unsupported status 3601; this is separate from HCI completion and cannot be replaced by a fake controller response."
      }
    ]
